            <title>[LU-21024] review-dne-zfs-part-1: sanity session timeout after 604 minutes during test_398b, slow run</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21024</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;review-dne-zfs-part-1 (RHEL 9.8, ZFS) hit the session limit while sanity test_398b was running. The test was not hung: fio was still doing I/O, slowly (about 500 KiB/s). sanity itself took over 8 hours on this run.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/1f8d3369-13c8-4e79-839c-774228832438" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/1f8d3369-13c8-4e79-839c-774228832438&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;sanity started:   21:57:45
test_398b start:  06:10:52
Timeout occurred after 604 minutes, last suite running was sanity
READ: bw=507KiB/s ... WRITE: bw=534KiB/s
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_398b had no failures in its last 73 review runs. This looks like slow test nodes, not a hang in 398b.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
